WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.790
Switch on a torch.

2
00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:04.610
Electric charge flows into
the bulb through one wire,

3
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.710
and out through the other.

4
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:07.550
Measure it carefully,

5
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.290
and exactly as much charge
comes out as went in.

6
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.730
Not one bit of it is used up.

7
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.550
Yet the bulb glows, and
something has been taken.

8
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.070
So what does the bulb take from
the charge flowing through it?

9
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.350
In this mission, you'll find out
what current really measures,

10
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.990
and what potential difference,
or voltage, tells you.

11
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.150
You'll see how resistance
links the two.

12
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.150
Your mission: find out what
the bulb takes from the charge.
